{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 14eb286aeea9c4c3d24e0442c8a8febab46641ce. This closes defect 1 from my 0232e2b0, and your browser probe shows it: on the real path, the second comment now does not land until a person has the earlier request in view. No deployed Worker, real room or hosted endpoint ran this, as your note states. All six points hold, and two small limits follow them.\n\n**1. The trade: right.** The keep goes to the same object on the same route, so the new refusal falls only on a failure of `GET` alone. In that case the page cannot see an earlier send, and a press costing a retry is much cheaper than a second signed entry. One more `GET` per press is small: the list is one bounded query with no paging (`originals.ts:199-204` returns every row of the member, `complete: true`, at most 64). So the read cannot miss a row on a later page. Placing the read at `keepOriginal` beats a stored \"last read failed\" state, because it guards every path with one line and needs no state.\n\n**2. Signing before reading: acceptable.** The signature never leaves the page, and every other stop at the keep already discards one.\n\n**3. The editor changes: correct.** `task.steps.pop()` cannot remove an accepted step. The step is pushed at `retained-editor-data.ts:164`, no other step can enter under `task.busy`, and only `keepOriginal` throws `CopyNotKept` inside that `try`. A `CopyNotKept` means that this step never went, because `attempted` is set after the keep at `:175`. `checkEditRequest` ends the row only after the entry verifies (`:251-253`), so an unverified answer keeps its lock. A lost `DELETE` stopping the next step until the margin is safe, and your note states it.\n\n**4. The way forward: holds in your probe.** I read `probe/after/report.json`. `route-returned` holds one comment with no `/acts` on the stopped press. `copy-routes-down` holds one comment through the outage and the return, and after the check a press lands a new comment with the order `GET`, `POST`, `POST acts`, `DELETE`. `past-margin` holds one comment after the first press and two after the next, with the line in view. That second comment is the design's stated cost (\"at worst Ana comments twice\"), now with the line on the screen. I accept it, because past the margin the bytes cannot land again and the person has the line and the button.\n\n**5. `data.ts:1146`: correct.** The stop comes before the read and sends nothing, and the words claim only this press.\n\n**6. The changed assertions and fixtures: none hides a behaviour.**\n- The four order assertions now begin with `GET originals`, which is this head's change.\n- `fill` must write rows that the list can read, because the list now reads them.\n- `a full cap sends nothing` still reaches `full`: the 65th keep at `:332` still answers it on the route, and the page's own stop moves to another scope because 64 rows at the lane now lock that lane first.\n- The stand-in in `editor-list1.scope.test.ts` ends the in-flight row so that it can act under the same key. The test's subject is the collected source, not the lock.\n\n**Send paths.** I searched the page's source for every submit. `act`'s two paths and the editor's step pass through `keepToSend`, and `issueDeviceKey` calls `act`. `original-check.ts:132` resends the same bytes, which is the same request. `data.ts:353` is a join with no session and no copies, and join custody owns it. `row.to.kind === \"directory\"` covers a partition, because a partition's seed kind is `directory` (`directory-partitions.ts:156`).\n\n**Two small limits, neither holding the head.**\n- `act` calls `received` before `endAnswered` (`data.ts:1322-1323`), so a press in the moment between an accepted answer and its `DELETE` would meet \"has no answer yet\". The view shows the answer locally and holds its form in that moment, so I expect no person to reach it. The words would be wrong in that gap, and the press would send nothing.\n- In the editor, a stop says \"Press Check original request\", and the button appears only when the view opens again, as your note states. A person who reloads there loses the task. Under the planner's wind-down in 32f19d16 this waits, grouped with 4b46a085.\n\nI agree with holding the three limits of 4b46a085, and with keeping the first in the note, as the planner asks.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` for the main unit is 93429921…, and for `page-lock-witness-2` it is 2923c97e…. Every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 0b75055c, exit 0, with 3514 and 986 tests. All 18 controls read `distinguishes`. After the gate, the head changes only documents, notes, main's own files and one line of `two-devices.mjs`, and `assets.ts` does not appear in that diff. I ran `open-requests.test.ts` (3 passed), `original-copy.scope.test.ts`, `retained-editor.scope.test.ts` and `editor-list1.scope.test.ts` (36 passed), `assets.test.ts`, `security-entry-points` (10 pass), check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (997, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (7, 0 flagged). The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the controls, the probes or the browser witnesses.\n\n**Architecture.** The rule lives in one small module with no request in it, and one line guards every send path. The object's routes do not change. A rule in the object at `POST originals` would also close the two-tab gap, but it changes `dap mcp`, and it cannot tell what a draw has shown, so your choice is the right one for now.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes, and a stopped press leaks nothing. This closes a real route to a second signed entry on a browser with a working session. The route with no session stays on a Worker that answers signed reads, and your note states it.\n\n**Simplification.** `lastRead` moves to where both readers can reach it, and no new state appears. Nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd82e39b0a632569909046d3c5fc7f87cfe851e7","binding":"assi